1
00:00:00,860 --> 00:00:02,680
Wealth, Fame, Power.

2
00:00:02,980 --> 00:00:04,597
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates,

3
00:00:04,680 --> 00:00:07,237
attained this and everything
else the world had to offer,

4
00:00:07,320 --> 00:00:10,496
and his dying words drove
countless souls to the seas.

5
00:00:10,740 --> 00:00:11,975
You want my treasure?

6
00:00:12,240 --> 00:00:13,440
You can have it.

7
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:16,680
I left everything I gathered
together in one place.

8
00:00:16,900 --> 00:00:19,080
Now you just have to find it.

9
00:00:20,960 --> 00:00:24,257
These words lured men to
the Grand Line in pursuit

10
00:00:24,340 --> 00:00:26,697
of dreams greater than
they'd ever dared to imagine.

11
00:00:26,780 --> 00:00:29,537
This is the time known
as the Great Pirate Era.

12
00:00:29,620 --> 00:00:35,000
Come aboard and bring along
all your hopes and dreams.

13
00:00:35,720 --> 00:00:40,360
Together we will find everything
that we're looking for!

14
00:00:41,540 --> 00:00:42,700
One piece.

15
00:00:48,020 --> 00:00:52,617
Compass left behind,
it'll only slow us down.

16
00:00:52,700 --> 00:00:58,437
Your heart will be your guide,
raise the sails and take the helm.

17
00:00:58,520 --> 00:01:01,117
That legendary place!

18
00:01:01,200 --> 00:01:03,817
That the end of the map reveals?

19
00:01:03,900 --> 00:01:06,717
Is only legendary.

20
00:01:06,800 --> 00:01:10,137
Till someone proves it real.

21
00:01:10,220 --> 00:01:12,577
Through it all!

22
00:01:12,660 --> 00:01:14,457
Through all the trouble of times!

23
00:01:14,540 --> 00:01:15,737
Through the heartache!

24
00:01:15,820 --> 00:01:16,837
And through the pain!

25
00:01:16,920 --> 00:01:19,577
Know that I will be there!

26
00:01:19,660 --> 00:01:21,397
To stand by you!

27
00:01:21,480 --> 00:01:24,220
Like I know you'll stand by me!

28
00:01:25,360 --> 00:01:26,817
So come aboard!

29
00:01:26,900 --> 00:01:30,940
And bring along all your hopes and dreams.

30
00:01:31,440 --> 00:01:36,080
Together we will find everything
that we're looking for!

31
00:01:37,260 --> 00:01:39,737
There's always room for you!

32
00:01:39,820 --> 00:01:42,520
If you want to be my friend!

33
00:01:43,140 --> 00:01:46,760
We are, we are on the crew!

34
00:01:48,480 --> 00:01:49,740
We are!

35
00:01:53,040 --> 00:01:55,277
Okay, so tell us all about it?

36
00:01:55,360 --> 00:01:57,020
I gotta admit, I'm curious.

37
00:01:57,400 --> 00:01:59,120
I'll pass. Hey, wait!

38
00:01:59,400 --> 00:02:01,047
I don't care about our past.

39
00:02:01,260 --> 00:02:03,660
Where are you going, Luffy? For a walk.

40
00:02:04,180 --> 00:02:05,010
A walk?

41
00:02:05,093 --> 00:02:07,197
Do you mean you're not
gonna listen to this?

42
00:02:07,280 --> 00:02:08,110
Nope.

43
00:02:10,080 --> 00:02:10,910
Who's he?

44
00:02:12,020 --> 00:02:13,040
Don't mind him.

45
00:02:13,200 --> 00:02:14,494
That's just how he is.

46
00:02:15,920 --> 00:02:17,038
We'll hear you out.

47
00:02:17,180 --> 00:02:20,237
Though I can tell you right now, I
don't think it's gonna change anything.

48
00:02:20,320 --> 00:02:21,857
Well, I'll listen, too.

49
00:02:21,940 --> 00:02:26,077
It might help me make some sense out of
everything that's going on around here.

50
00:02:26,160 --> 00:02:26,990
Me too.

51
00:02:27,100 --> 00:02:28,940
I want to know all about her.

52
00:02:30,840 --> 00:02:32,640
Now he's asleep. Hey!

53
00:02:32,820 --> 00:02:34,467
You said you'd hear her out!

54
00:02:37,980 --> 00:02:39,377
Hmm, I see.

55
00:02:39,460 --> 00:02:41,380
This is why it was hard for her.

56
00:02:47,700 --> 00:02:48,960
I fell asleep.

57
00:02:51,120 --> 00:02:52,857
Oh no, Nojiko.

58
00:02:52,940 --> 00:02:55,120
I wonder where she ran off to.

59
00:03:03,200 --> 00:03:05,737
Just a little more, Bellomere.

60
00:03:05,820 --> 00:03:09,200
Just a little more and
everything will be ours again.

61
00:03:10,720 --> 00:03:13,980
Cocoyashi village, the
tangerine farm, everything.

62
00:03:20,640 --> 00:03:23,320
It's taken eight years.

63
00:03:34,240 --> 00:03:35,597
It's done!

64
00:03:35,680 --> 00:03:36,920
It's done!

65
00:03:37,600 --> 00:03:38,440
Yay!

66
00:03:44,960 --> 00:03:47,620
Now if I could just get that book.

67
00:03:57,980 --> 00:03:59,460
Hey, is that you, Nami?

68
00:03:59,660 --> 00:04:01,248
Do you need any help there?

69
00:04:02,500 --> 00:04:03,960
No, I'm just looking.

70
00:04:04,280 --> 00:04:05,660
I'll be going now.

71
00:04:15,940 --> 00:04:17,000
That's too bad.

72
00:04:17,580 --> 00:04:18,860
Damn it, Nami!

73
00:04:18,960 --> 00:04:23,017
Not again, Sticky Fingers.

74
00:04:23,100 --> 00:04:28,977
You little urchin.

75
00:04:29,060 --> 00:04:32,017
How many times do I have to
tell you that stealing is wrong?

76
00:04:32,100 --> 00:04:34,617
How else am I gonna get what I need?

77
00:04:34,700 --> 00:04:36,053
I don't have any money.

78
00:04:37,320 --> 00:04:38,150
Chipscake!

79
00:04:40,760 --> 00:04:41,920
Bellamy! Bellamy!

80
00:04:42,320 --> 00:04:43,967
I caught her stealing again!

81
00:04:44,160 --> 00:04:45,500
Now open up this door!

82
00:04:49,640 --> 00:04:50,960
What do you want now?

83
00:04:51,380 --> 00:04:52,340
You're back.

84
00:04:52,600 --> 00:04:53,857
That was a quick trip.

85
00:04:53,940 --> 00:04:54,940
I got a ride.

86
00:04:55,380 --> 00:04:59,840
Listen, you better get control of her
before she winds up in a jail cell.

87
00:05:00,780 --> 00:05:02,260
Thanks for the advice.

88
00:05:02,920 --> 00:05:06,277
Haven't you ever seen something
you've wanted and just taken it?

89
00:05:06,360 --> 00:05:08,417
You're the reason she acts this way!

90
00:05:08,500 --> 00:05:10,080
Relax, I'm just kidding.

91
00:05:10,500 --> 00:05:13,029
I hope you were kind
enough to pay for her.

92
00:05:13,520 --> 00:05:14,540
Uh, Bellamere?

93
00:05:15,300 --> 00:05:16,457
Thanks so much.

94
00:05:16,540 --> 00:05:18,297
I don't have the money right now.

95
00:05:18,380 --> 00:05:19,556
I'll pay it somehow.

96
00:05:20,820 --> 00:05:22,680
Does that sound good?

97
00:05:24,100 --> 00:05:26,200
You can't say things like that!

98
00:05:28,780 --> 00:05:30,620
Look, he's as red as a beet!

99
00:05:35,960 --> 00:05:38,860
Now then, laugh it up
while you still can, Nami.

100
00:05:40,820 --> 00:05:41,860
I'm sorry.

101
00:05:42,740 --> 00:05:46,120
It's just that I really
need that book, Bellamere.

102
00:05:46,460 --> 00:05:49,578
Then why didn't you ask me
if I would buy it for you?

103
00:05:50,840 --> 00:05:52,899
Because I know you can't afford it.

104
00:05:53,140 --> 00:05:54,200
Of course I can.

105
00:05:54,460 --> 00:05:56,677
There's money left over
from the last harvest.

106
00:05:56,760 --> 00:05:58,357
But I heard them in the village.

107
00:05:58,440 --> 00:06:00,917
They said the weather's
been so good lately?

108
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:04,757
That everyone's tangerines will sell,
Which means we can't raise our price!

109
00:06:04,840 --> 00:06:06,717
or we may not be able to sell at all.

110
00:06:06,800 --> 00:06:08,957
They don't know what
they're talking about.

111
00:06:09,040 --> 00:06:10,280
Way to go, Nami.

112
00:06:10,800 --> 00:06:14,329
If I had stolen it, there's no
way I would have been caught.

113
00:06:15,540 --> 00:06:17,380
No more stealing, right?

114
00:06:17,740 --> 00:06:20,200
I was just joking, that's all.

115
00:06:20,560 --> 00:06:21,840
That really hurt.

116
00:06:26,740 --> 00:06:28,697
I'm sorry, but one thing's for sure.

117
00:06:28,780 --> 00:06:31,680
The maps you draw are so amazing, Nami!

118
00:06:33,380 --> 00:06:36,720
I see you can draw land maps
now as well as sea charts.

119
00:06:37,980 --> 00:06:40,380
That's the map of our island, isn't it?

120
00:06:41,820 --> 00:06:45,879
Nobody will believe that such a
little girl drew this all by herself.

121
00:06:46,960 --> 00:06:50,607
I wanted the book so I'd be able
to start studying navigation.

122
00:06:51,340 --> 00:06:52,480
Navigation as well?

123
00:06:52,740 --> 00:06:55,460
You're going to be a
navigator? That's right.

124
00:06:55,660 --> 00:06:58,817
I'm going to guide ships around
all the oceans of the world.

125
00:06:58,900 --> 00:06:59,782
It'll be great.

126
00:07:00,740 --> 00:07:04,505
And I'll be able to make maps of
all the far-off places I'll go.

127
00:07:05,860 --> 00:07:09,377
So, this island map is a first
step toward realizing your dream.

128
00:07:09,460 --> 00:07:10,290
Is that it?

129
00:07:11,080 --> 00:07:11,910
Mm-hmm.

130
00:07:13,040 --> 00:07:14,700
A world map, huh?

131
00:07:15,580 --> 00:07:17,637
Nami, your dream is going to come true.

132
00:07:17,720 --> 00:07:19,000
I have no doubt.

133
00:07:30,060 --> 00:07:31,400
Hey, Othellamere. Hmm?

134
00:07:31,600 --> 00:07:34,137
Why haven't you been eating
dinner with us lately?

135
00:07:34,220 --> 00:07:35,867
I've been eating tangerines.

136
00:07:36,080 --> 00:07:38,260
I've just been on a diet, that's all.

137
00:07:38,500 --> 00:07:40,382
Then I don't want to eat either.

138
00:07:40,480 --> 00:07:42,097
What's with all of the drama?

139
00:07:42,180 --> 00:07:44,597
You need to eat because
you are a growing girl.

140
00:07:44,680 --> 00:07:46,217
Why do you keep lying to us?

141
00:07:46,300 --> 00:07:49,137
You're not eating because we don't
have enough money to buy food.

142
00:07:49,220 --> 00:07:50,820
That's why. Really?

143
00:07:51,140 --> 00:07:54,199
You're starving yourself
so that we won't go hungry.

144
00:07:54,760 --> 00:07:58,137
Tangerines replenish my skin with
the power of liquid sunlight.

145
00:07:58,220 --> 00:08:01,297
And they are the only reason I
am still such a ravishing beauty,

146
00:08:01,380 --> 00:08:03,820
even though I am in my extreme late 20s.

147
00:08:04,080 --> 00:08:05,757
But your hands are all yellow.

148
00:08:05,840 --> 00:08:08,722
Would you just shut up
and eat your food already?

149
00:08:09,420 --> 00:08:10,940
And here you go, Nami.

150
00:08:11,160 --> 00:08:12,000
All done.

151
00:08:12,100 --> 00:08:14,840
A Bellamere one-of-a-kind
original. Oh, great.

152
00:08:14,980 --> 00:08:15,837
A hand-me-down.

153
00:08:15,920 --> 00:08:17,017
Yeah, that's true.

154
00:08:17,100 --> 00:08:18,960
But it suits you. See, look.

155
00:08:19,460 --> 00:08:21,580
But the lion used to be a sunflower.

156
00:08:22,180 --> 00:08:23,077
Quit complaining.

157
00:08:23,160 --> 00:08:26,577
You have to take my hand-me-downs
or you won't get any new clothes.

158
00:08:26,660 --> 00:08:27,657
But it's not fair.

159
00:08:27,740 --> 00:08:30,737
You get new clothes all the
time and mine are all used.

160
00:08:30,820 --> 00:08:32,702
I get old clothes too, you know.

161
00:08:32,840 --> 00:08:35,537
So just suck it up, Nami,
and take what you get.

162
00:08:35,620 --> 00:08:36,450
Understand?

163
00:08:36,560 --> 00:08:39,148
We didn't come from the
same parents anyway.

164
00:08:39,260 --> 00:08:41,580
We're not real sisters, so who cares?

165
00:08:42,400 --> 00:08:43,230
Nami!

166
00:08:51,720 --> 00:08:52,779
Bellamere, please!

167
00:08:58,800 --> 00:09:01,329
So what if you don't
have the same parents?

168
00:09:04,320 --> 00:09:07,791
I don't ever want to hear you
say anything like that again!

169
00:09:08,460 --> 00:09:09,860
I don't care.

170
00:09:10,460 --> 00:09:12,217
You're not even our real mother!

171
00:09:12,300 --> 00:09:14,617
You're just some lady
who's taking care of us.

172
00:09:14,700 --> 00:09:19,229
You wish we'd never come here so you
could buy clothes and food for yourself.

173
00:09:19,380 --> 00:09:21,737
You'd be better off
without us, wouldn't you?

174
00:09:21,820 --> 00:09:25,055
That way you could be selfish
and do whatever you want.

175
00:09:25,360 --> 00:09:26,320
I wish...

176
00:09:27,060 --> 00:09:31,648
I wish that one rich would have adopted
us instead of a sneaky loser like you!

177
00:09:39,640 --> 00:09:40,600
Well, fine.

178
00:09:41,780 --> 00:09:46,217
If you hate it here so much, you can go
find someplace else to live if you want.

179
00:09:46,300 --> 00:09:47,829
I didn't sign up for this.

180
00:09:48,120 --> 00:09:49,000
Stop fighting!

181
00:09:49,200 --> 00:09:50,259
Please, just stop!

182
00:09:50,860 --> 00:09:52,540
I'm never coming back!

183
00:09:53,420 --> 00:09:55,540
Stop! Stop! Stop!

184
00:10:05,800 --> 00:10:08,137
Valamere, the three of us are a family.

185
00:10:08,220 --> 00:10:09,260
That's the truth!

186
00:10:09,900 --> 00:10:13,880
And you know Nami feels the
same, no matter what she said.

187
00:10:15,820 --> 00:10:17,702
Look who's being the adult here.

188
00:10:17,960 --> 00:10:20,489
I blew up, and you're
the level-headed one.

189
00:10:21,340 --> 00:10:23,164
Why don't you go and find Nami?

190
00:10:23,460 --> 00:10:27,519
I'll make something special for
dinner, and we can all make up, okay?

191
00:10:41,820 --> 00:10:42,650
Sorry, lady.

192
00:10:42,740 --> 00:10:44,717
Two for five is the
lowest price I can offer.

193
00:10:44,800 --> 00:10:46,800
Isn't that really your best offer?

194
00:10:47,620 --> 00:10:48,580
Half off.

195
00:10:48,740 --> 00:10:49,600
Today only.

196
00:10:49,920 --> 00:10:50,757
Fresh produce.

197
00:10:50,840 --> 00:10:53,337
You won't find a lower
price anywhere today.

198
00:10:53,420 --> 00:10:55,538
I guarantee it or you're money back.

199
00:11:03,860 --> 00:11:06,757
So you've run away from home
and come to the village.

200
00:11:06,840 --> 00:11:08,020
Now what's the plan?

201
00:11:10,480 --> 00:11:12,160
Drink before it gets cold.

202
00:11:15,320 --> 00:11:19,537
Bellamere would be so much happier if
she didn't have to take care of us?

203
00:11:19,620 --> 00:11:21,208
And why would you say that?

204
00:11:21,960 --> 00:11:24,537
Well, you need a lot of money
to take care of two kids.

205
00:11:24,620 --> 00:11:28,437
And because of me, the whole
village hates her right now.

206
00:11:28,520 --> 00:11:29,820
That's progress.

207
00:11:30,360 --> 00:11:32,419
At least you're considering others.

208
00:11:33,520 --> 00:11:34,457
But don't worry.

209
00:11:34,540 --> 00:11:37,417
When Bellamere was your age,
he was a complete nightmare.

210
00:11:37,500 --> 00:11:39,324
terrorizing the entire village.

211
00:11:39,480 --> 00:11:41,280
Is that the truth? Sure.

212
00:11:41,620 --> 00:11:45,267
Even now the villagers look at
her as some kind of a Scrap.

213
00:11:45,480 --> 00:11:49,477
So you can imagine how surprised everyone
in the village was when she joined up?

214
00:11:49,560 --> 00:11:50,854
with the marines, huh?

215
00:11:51,160 --> 00:11:51,990
Marines?

216
00:11:52,073 --> 00:11:55,240
You mean Bellamere was in
the marines? That's right.

217
00:12:03,940 --> 00:12:08,822
She said she couldn't stand by and do
nothing while pirates killed innocent people.

218
00:12:09,260 --> 00:12:10,940
Then she left the village.

219
00:12:18,420 --> 00:12:22,740
She was teetering on the
verge of death when...

220
00:12:23,580 --> 00:12:27,320
If this is the end, then so be it.

221
00:12:45,060 --> 00:12:46,780
Your little sister?

222
00:12:51,460 --> 00:12:52,760
Uh-uh.

223
00:12:53,160 --> 00:12:54,260
I found her.

224
00:13:04,040 --> 00:13:05,740
How did she survive?

225
00:13:21,080 --> 00:13:23,940
That innocent child was you, Nami.

226
00:13:25,140 --> 00:13:29,787
And seeing how precious you were gave
Bellamy the right reasons to live again.

227
00:13:40,360 --> 00:13:42,560
It is a ship! I knew it!

228
00:13:42,660 --> 00:13:45,660
Who on earth would be out
in such a terrible storm?

229
00:13:55,540 --> 00:13:56,370
Doctor.

230
00:13:56,453 --> 00:13:57,300
I need a doctor.

231
00:13:57,720 --> 00:13:58,820
What's going on?

232
00:13:58,960 --> 00:14:00,842
What happened to you, Bellamere?

233
00:14:01,060 --> 00:14:01,890
Bellamere!

234
00:14:01,973 --> 00:14:03,444
Did somebody call for a doctor?

235
00:14:06,120 --> 00:14:08,240
Who are these children? Doctor!

236
00:14:08,480 --> 00:14:09,317
They're burning up.

237
00:14:09,400 --> 00:14:11,137
I'm afraid they might be really sick.

238
00:14:11,220 --> 00:14:12,257
Please, help them.

239
00:14:12,340 --> 00:14:13,222
Give them here.

240
00:14:15,340 --> 00:14:19,557
All right, and we'd better mend up those
nasty wounds of yours as well, young lady.

241
00:14:19,640 --> 00:14:20,660
Never mind me!

242
00:14:21,140 --> 00:14:22,877
Please, just don't let them die.

243
00:14:22,960 --> 00:14:24,177
You have to save me.

244
00:14:24,260 --> 00:14:26,477
Him I'm begging

245
00:14:26,560 --> 00:14:33,257
you doctor I don't

246
00:14:33,340 --> 00:14:35,637
believe it say that whole thing again

247
00:14:35,720 --> 00:14:39,877
I said I'm gonna try To be the mother
of these two girls it's that simple

248
00:14:39,960 --> 00:14:44,797
no way that's insane you are far
too Immature to handle this much

249
00:14:44,880 --> 00:14:49,997
responsibility you can't handle them by
yourself just hand them over to the...

250
00:14:50,080 --> 00:14:51,160
I've made my mind!

251
00:14:52,100 --> 00:14:53,997
You can't deny that I'm an adult,

252
00:14:54,080 --> 00:14:56,197
and what I've lived through
as a Marine has given

253
00:14:56,280 --> 00:14:58,557
me the right to be
treated with more respect.

254
00:14:58,640 --> 00:15:01,934
I'm perfectly capable of
taking care of these two girls.

255
00:15:02,380 --> 00:15:05,277
And nothing can stop me from
raising them to be wonderful.

256
00:15:05,360 --> 00:15:06,190
girls.

257
00:15:07,940 --> 00:15:10,469
So now we're going to
be a family together.

258
00:15:10,740 --> 00:15:13,620
Nami and Nochiko have
renewed my love of life.

259
00:15:18,740 --> 00:15:23,420
The bond between the three of you girls
goes far deeper than any normal family.

260
00:15:27,860 --> 00:15:30,880
Mommy, I thought I'd
find you here. Nojiko?

261
00:15:31,760 --> 00:15:34,260
Come on, Bellomere's waiting for us.

262
00:15:34,500 --> 00:15:36,480
She's making us a special supper.

263
00:15:38,920 --> 00:15:39,750
Sure.

264
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:41,817
I think she's making your favorite.

265
00:15:41,900 --> 00:15:43,724
Omelettes are good to eat, son!

266
00:15:46,580 --> 00:15:49,500
I love omelettes! Alright!

267
00:15:54,940 --> 00:15:56,900
The pirates are coming!

268
00:15:57,120 --> 00:15:58,160
Everybody run!

269
00:16:00,660 --> 00:16:02,720
The pirates are coming!

270
00:16:02,980 --> 00:16:03,860
Hide!

271
00:16:14,780 --> 00:16:17,100
The Arlong Pirates! Arlong?

272
00:16:17,240 --> 00:16:18,299
That's impossible!

273
00:16:18,520 --> 00:16:21,237
Why would Fishman from
the Grand Line come here?

274
00:16:21,320 --> 00:16:24,997
The rumor about the split between
the Fishman and Pirates must be true!

275
00:16:25,080 --> 00:16:27,320
Nami! Nojiko! Genzo!

276
00:16:28,240 --> 00:16:30,122
It's too dangerous for you here.

277
00:16:30,300 --> 00:16:31,535
Go hide in the woods.

278
00:16:32,060 --> 00:16:34,440
What about... You must go! Now!

279
00:16:45,640 --> 00:16:49,040
Greetings and salutations,
you pathetic little humans.

280
00:16:49,380 --> 00:16:54,321
From this moment on, this entire island and
its inhabitants are a part of my domain.

281
00:16:56,160 --> 00:16:57,380
Listen closely.

282
00:16:57,740 --> 00:17:02,420
From now on, on the first day of every
month, you will buy your lives from me.

283
00:17:04,860 --> 00:17:08,820
100,000 berries for adults,
50,000 for children.

284
00:17:09,300 --> 00:17:11,620
Those who cannot pay will die.

285
00:17:14,020 --> 00:17:15,660
What should we do, Nojiko?

286
00:17:16,740 --> 00:17:18,800
We don't have that much money.

287
00:17:19,040 --> 00:17:21,617
Maybe the fishmen won't
be able to find our house.

288
00:17:21,700 --> 00:17:23,288
You can't see it from here.

289
00:17:28,400 --> 00:17:29,380
Is that it?

290
00:17:29,560 --> 00:17:30,760
So what's the haul?

291
00:17:30,980 --> 00:17:33,340
About 25 million, give or take.

292
00:17:34,040 --> 00:17:35,520
You all shall live.

293
00:17:39,340 --> 00:17:42,297
It looks like we each have
to pay 100,000 berries

294
00:17:42,380 --> 00:17:45,580
to these fishmen every
month just to stay alive No,

295
00:17:45,840 --> 00:17:49,717
there's no way we could survive We
don't have a choice We should just be

296
00:17:49,800 --> 00:17:54,197
happy that nobody in the village has been
killed yet If all they want is money,

297
00:17:54,280 --> 00:17:55,868
that's an easy price to pay

298
00:17:57,280 --> 00:18:02,117
I just hope they leave without noticing
Bellamere's house With two children,

299
00:18:02,200 --> 00:18:04,080
she'd need 200,000 berries

300
00:18:04,740 --> 00:18:07,034
There's no way she has that much saved.

301
00:18:09,400 --> 00:18:10,960
It's time to leave.

302
00:18:11,480 --> 00:18:12,600
Come, brothers.

303
00:18:16,540 --> 00:18:19,716
Arlong, there's smoke coming
from outside the village.

304
00:18:26,640 --> 00:18:27,470
Okay.

305
00:18:27,553 --> 00:18:28,383
Let's see.

306
00:18:29,000 --> 00:18:29,830
Delicious.

307
00:18:29,913 --> 00:18:33,522
There isn't anything quite as tasty
as my special tangerine sauce.

308
00:18:33,940 --> 00:18:36,040
Nami and Nojiko are gonna love it.

309
00:18:36,280 --> 00:18:39,221
It looks like chimney smoke
from somebody's house.

310
00:18:40,340 --> 00:18:42,920
Oh, we almost missed that one.

311
00:18:45,520 --> 00:18:46,350
Bellomir!

312
00:18:46,760 --> 00:18:48,740
All right, let's go, guys.

313
00:18:51,360 --> 00:18:52,460
This is bad.

314
00:18:52,740 --> 00:18:55,211
The pirates are going to Bellomir's house!

315
00:18:59,460 --> 00:19:00,380
Genzo, look!

316
00:19:00,520 --> 00:19:01,857
Nojiko and Nami are gone!

317
00:19:01,940 --> 00:19:02,770
What did you say?

318
00:19:02,853 --> 00:19:07,640
I think the duck needs another ten
minutes and the stew is almost ready.

319
00:19:07,960 --> 00:19:10,057
This is definitely
going to blow my budget,

320
00:19:10,140 --> 00:19:12,611
but sometimes you've got to live a little.

321
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:24,830
Bellamere!

322
00:19:24,913 --> 00:19:25,743
Bellamere!

323
00:19:25,826 --> 00:19:26,944
Bellamere's going to be killed!

324
00:19:33,720 --> 00:19:36,380
We will not abandon Villamir!

325
00:19:37,000 --> 00:19:37,830
Damn it!

326
00:19:38,100 --> 00:19:39,276
Why did this happen?

327
00:19:39,380 --> 00:19:40,860
Hold on, Villamir!

328
00:19:44,560 --> 00:19:46,140
Oh, they're here.

329
00:19:54,080 --> 00:19:55,180
It's open!

330
00:19:55,600 --> 00:19:56,560
Come in!

331
00:19:57,420 --> 00:19:58,250
Why, thanks!

332
00:20:22,560 --> 00:20:25,266
I guess you weren't
expecting a former marine.

333
00:20:26,700 --> 00:20:30,935
Now what would a pirate from the Grand
Line want with Cocoyashi Village?

334
00:20:37,060 --> 00:20:38,400
What's so funny?

335
00:20:45,440 --> 00:20:48,940
Useless, foolish,
stupid, empty, worthless.

336
00:20:49,580 --> 00:20:53,780
All of you humans, you have
no strength to speak on.

337
00:21:01,260 --> 00:21:03,737
We'll help her escape
through the back door!

338
00:21:03,820 --> 00:21:05,857
What if the pirates are already there?

339
00:21:05,940 --> 00:21:07,120
It'll be okay! Stop!

340
00:21:11,680 --> 00:21:12,510
Doctor!

341
00:21:12,593 --> 00:21:14,520
You can't go back home! What?

342
00:21:14,760 --> 00:21:16,540
But we have to save Bellamere!

343
00:21:16,700 --> 00:21:19,120
No, Gecko, Nami, quiet and listen to me.

344
00:21:19,560 --> 00:21:20,736
There will be times.

345
00:21:20,900 --> 00:21:23,180
Times in life like this moment now.

346
00:21:23,780 --> 00:21:27,721
When you have to learn the truth,
no matter how hard it is to take.

347
00:21:41,180 --> 00:21:42,400
It's no use.

348
00:21:42,600 --> 00:21:46,480
These guys are real monsters,
and I'm going to die.

349
00:21:47,140 --> 00:21:47,970
No, Chico.

350
00:21:48,360 --> 00:21:49,190
No, me.

351
00:21:49,560 --> 00:21:53,440
Bellamy, don't waste your life
because you're a stubborn fool.

352
00:21:53,780 --> 00:21:55,697
There's no reason for
this fight when it can

353
00:21:55,780 --> 00:21:58,368
be resolved with a
simple exchange of money.

354
00:22:00,720 --> 00:22:02,920
Just pay the fee, and I'll stop.

355
00:22:03,420 --> 00:22:06,773
$100,000 for each adult and
$50,000 for each kid, if any.

356
00:22:06,860 --> 00:22:11,420
If you can pay for your whole family,
I'd gladly spare your lives. Family?

357
00:22:14,460 --> 00:22:16,048
How much money do you have?

358
00:22:16,400 --> 00:22:18,140
You need $200,000.

359
00:22:19,760 --> 00:22:20,920
I don't have it.

360
00:22:21,800 --> 00:22:23,200
I'm not even close.

361
00:22:25,140 --> 00:22:27,880
Hey, the table is set for three in here?

362
00:22:30,140 --> 00:22:31,980
A family of three.

363
00:22:34,160 --> 00:22:35,880
It's for me and my friend.

364
00:22:37,740 --> 00:22:40,177
We were supposed to have
a nice dinner tonight.

365
00:22:40,260 --> 00:22:42,000
Before you came.

366
00:22:42,880 --> 00:22:43,877
Come, Bellamere!

367
00:22:43,960 --> 00:22:45,977
I know you've made something wonderful.

368
00:22:46,060 --> 00:22:48,397
Pay them before our food gets cold.

369
00:22:48,480 --> 00:22:50,877
Just pay the pirates.

370
00:22:50,960 --> 00:22:53,160
And then they'll leave us alone.

371
00:22:53,760 --> 00:22:55,500
Now everyone is saved!

372
00:22:56,580 --> 00:22:57,437
It's true!

373
00:22:57,520 --> 00:23:01,579
The village register shows no record
of her marrying or giving birth.

374
00:23:02,300 --> 00:23:03,800
She's always been single.

375
00:23:08,260 --> 00:23:09,090
Listen!

376
00:23:09,173 --> 00:23:12,777
There's no way that the pirates
will ever find out about you.

377
00:23:12,860 --> 00:23:15,577
But you have to leave
this island immediately!

378
00:23:15,660 --> 00:23:17,597
And don't ever look back!

379
00:23:17,680 --> 00:23:20,657
It's the only way for all
three of you to survive!

380
00:23:20,740 --> 00:23:23,117
We can't afford it any other way!

381
00:23:23,200 --> 00:23:25,757
You're much too young to be at sea alone!

382
00:23:25,840 --> 00:23:27,197
But you've survived before!

383
00:23:27,280 --> 00:23:29,280
And if there's even a chance! No!

384
00:23:30,580 --> 00:23:32,000
I don't want to!

385
00:23:33,240 --> 00:23:35,517
I want to stay in this village!

386
00:23:35,600 --> 00:23:37,220
It's because!

387
00:23:37,900 --> 00:23:38,937
We're poor!

388
00:23:39,020 --> 00:23:41,020
That's why we can't stay together.

389
00:23:42,500 --> 00:23:43,330
Why?

390
00:23:43,480 --> 00:23:45,127
Why can't they just go away?

391
00:23:47,780 --> 00:23:48,680
Well then.

392
00:23:49,400 --> 00:23:51,137
Now we can all be safe.

393
00:23:51,220 --> 00:23:53,100
Fine, we'll leave this island.

394
00:23:53,820 --> 00:23:56,560
We have to leave or Pelomir will die.

395
00:24:13,380 --> 00:24:15,840
Wait, who said I was paying for me?

396
00:24:17,360 --> 00:24:20,066
That money I gave up was
for my two daughters.

397
00:24:20,480 --> 00:24:22,320
But I can't pay you!

398
00:24:24,280 --> 00:24:26,540
What are you doing? It's okay.

399
00:24:27,380 --> 00:24:29,860
I have to do this for my family!

400
00:24:30,640 --> 00:24:32,680
Even if it costs me my life!

401
00:24:35,220 --> 00:24:36,177
Stupid girl.

402
00:24:36,260 --> 00:24:39,201
It's true the three of us
aren't related by blood.

403
00:24:40,500 --> 00:24:41,780
But we're family.

404
00:24:42,320 --> 00:24:44,920
All I've ever wanted
was to be their mother.

405
00:24:46,520 --> 00:24:49,620
And now, I can be.

406
00:24:50,680 --> 00:24:52,060
What? No!

407
00:24:53,220 --> 00:24:55,377
I wish that one rich would have adopted us

408
00:24:55,460 --> 00:24:59,020
instead of a stinky loser
like you It was a lie!

409
00:24:59,480 --> 00:25:01,560
I was lying, Bellamy!

410
00:25:16,780 --> 00:25:17,960
Don't cry, girls.

411
00:25:18,420 --> 00:25:19,377
I wish I could have...

412
00:25:19,460 --> 00:25:21,636
I could have provided for you better.

413
00:25:22,260 --> 00:25:26,240
I wish I could have been a
better mother to the both of you.

414
00:25:26,440 --> 00:25:27,340
Don't say that!

415
00:25:27,680 --> 00:25:28,877
We don't need anything!

416
00:25:28,960 --> 00:25:29,842
Just don't die!

417
00:25:30,000 --> 00:25:30,877
Don't leave us!

418
00:25:30,960 --> 00:25:32,417
You need to see the map!

419
00:25:32,500 --> 00:25:34,559
I'm going to drive the whole world!

420
00:25:36,280 --> 00:25:37,920
Yes, your map.

421
00:25:38,440 --> 00:25:40,480
Go and make your dreams come true.

422
00:25:44,040 --> 00:25:45,020
For me.

423
00:25:45,680 --> 00:25:47,000
Tha, I'm here now!

424
00:25:50,000 --> 00:25:51,660
So these are your daughters?

425
00:25:54,780 --> 00:25:55,960
Yeah, that's right.

426
00:25:56,440 --> 00:25:59,597
And you have promised me
that you'll leave them alone.

427
00:25:59,680 --> 00:26:03,480
No problem, as long as you
die like a good girl. Papa!

428
00:26:04,220 --> 00:26:05,050
AAAAAAAH!

429
00:26:15,120 --> 00:26:18,120
Well then, don't kill him, boys.

430
00:26:18,880 --> 00:26:21,040
No, just teach him a lesson.

431
00:26:21,400 --> 00:26:23,480
Now to set an example.

432
00:26:29,560 --> 00:26:31,360
You ready to die?

433
00:26:41,200 --> 00:26:43,200
Nojiko! Nami!

434
00:26:46,040 --> 00:26:47,380
Love you.
